BT 1 0 0 1 0 88 Tm 9.6 TL .145098 .164706 .180392 rg /F1+0 8 Tf 9.6 TL (Figure 1. Cross-dataset GSEA identifies consistent enrichment of the VIC osteogenic program.) Tj /F2+0 8 Tf 9.6 TL ( ) Tj /F1+0 8 Tf 9.6 TL (a) Tj /F2+0 8 Tf 9.6 TL ( Human valve transcriptomic) Tj T* (datasets: GSE51472 \(discovery; 5 normal and 5 calcified valves\), GSE51472 + GSE12644 \(ComBat-adjusted sensitivity analysis; 15) Tj T* (normal and 15 calcified valves\), and GSE83453 \(validation; 8 normal and 9 calcified tricuspid valves\). The sensitivity analysis) Tj T* (includes the discovery samples. Sclerotic valves in GSE51472 and bicuspid valves in GSE83453 were excluded. ) Tj /F1+0 8 Tf 9.6 TL (b) Tj /F2+0 8 Tf 9.6 TL ( Normalized) Tj T* (enrichment scores \(NES\) for five prespecified gene sets. Positive NES indicates enrichment in calcified valves. Symbols distinguish) Tj T* (analysis sets; filled symbols indicate Benjamini\001Hochberg-adjusted P < 0.05. Adjustment was performed across the five sets within) Tj T* (each analysis set. Strong consistency denotes concordant NES signs with adjusted P < 0.05 in at least two analysis sets; directional) Tj T* (consistency denotes concordant signs with fewer than two significant analysis sets; inconsistent denotes opposing signs. ) Tj /F1+0 8 Tf 9.6 TL (c) Tj  T* -0.064238 Tw /F2+0 8 Tf 9.6 TL (Membership of the ten genes in the union of osteogenic leading-edge subsets. Six genes were shared across all three subsets. Exact) Tj T* 0 Tw (results and gene membership are provided in Additional file 3: Tables S1 and S2.) Tj T* ET
